WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.480
We're deep into added time at the end of
the second half, and the score remains 1-1.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.490
This will probably be the last action 
of the game for Japan's Under-16s.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.730
Goal!

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.300
You know, I don't mind you celebrating...

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.420
Aoyama!

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.190
...but can you please not hug me and stuff?

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:06.570
You'll get me dirty.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.860
Aoyama-kun sure is a clean freak.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.480
<b>#01</b>

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.480
<b>Aoyama-kun Is a Clean Freak</b>

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.440
<b>Fujimi High School</b>

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.030
Aoyama-kyun...

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.030
So cool!

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.360
It's so clean!

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.530
I wish he'd wipe it every day!

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.130
Aoyama-kun!

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.250
Wow, it's so sparkly!

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.990
You're amazing, Aoyama!

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.060
Aoyama-kun!

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.530
<i>I get it, Aoyama.</i>

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.260
<i>Even as you clean, you feel like
the dirt keeps coming back,</i>

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.260
<i>leaving you in an endless loop
where you just keep cleaning forever.</i>

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.440
A-o-ya-ma!

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.150
Practice has already started.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:36.600
Zaizen-san...

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.840
You're already worn out!

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.820
Do you have enough in the tank for practice?!

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.030
I want to hear you guys!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:49.910
Yes, sir!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.270
Aoyama-kun!

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:58.170
What kind of soap are you using?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.530
Aoyama-kun, that's some 
impressive lathering!

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.470
Far post!

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.600
Keep your eyes on your man!

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:14.900
Here it comes!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.860
Aoyama-kun!

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.640
His hands are so clean.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.320
Look at his fingertips!

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.320
Damn you...

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:26.740
How long are you going to keep that up?

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.530
I'll kill you!

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.040
That's enough.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.920
Coach Miwa.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.530
Kaocchi, Aoyama's an extreme germaphobe.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.890
Could you please stop calling me that?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:53.850
Ah, it's all good.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.820
Just keep an eye out for him, as his senior.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:59.820
After all, you'll be linking up 
because of the positions you play.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:02.360
<i>"Linking up..."</i>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.450
Pass!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.700
Header!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:12.790
Eek!

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.600
<i>I don't see it working in the slightest,</i>

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.540
<i>but with him on the team, winning the 
district prelims isn't a pipe dream.</i>

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.010
Hey, Aoyama!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.760
Make sure you stay hydrated.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:29.890
No.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.920
Drink it!

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.350
I'd rather die.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:35.510
What?

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:38.690
I told you. He's a germaphobe.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:45.740
He won't use something if someone else
has touched or drank from it.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.490
Does he really have to wash it?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.160
Here it comes!

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.870
<i>Just you watch, Aoyama...</i>

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.700
It's a cross!

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.300
<i>I have the height advantage.</i>

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.290
<i>I'll jump higher than you and score!</i>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.760
<i>Why isn't he jumping?</i>

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:13.780
Gotcha!

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.220
Just leave the muscleheads to us.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.290
We got this.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.320
That was a blatant foul!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.250
Is it a throw-in?

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.190
I'll take it!

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:27.740
Thank you.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.310
What is this?

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.460
Don't get so worked up.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.330
That guy's kinda fun.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.060
Exactly. The real winners are
the ones who have the most fun.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.660
Keep it fun!

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.290
Aoyama-kun!

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:43.940
Here it comes!

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:58.130
If you think you can get away with 
everything just because you're good,

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.390
you're in for a rude awakening, you idiot!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.310
And you guys! Quit coddling him!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:04.820
You know what I mean!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:10.110
Dude, don't you realize
you're far more coddled than he is?

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.060
I mean, just look at those 
brand spanking new cleats.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.500
He's right! Coddle City!

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.610
I got these from my daddy—
I mean, my old man!

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.970
Oldest son of a business mogul?
What is your life, a TV show?!

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.610
Get outta here, Richie Rich!

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:30.580
And what is with that old butler
ferrying you to and from school?!

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:31.890
Yeah! Right on!

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.860
Try experiencing the crush of 
a morning rush hour train for once!

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:36.340
Amen!

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.770
<i>Seriously? I'm the more coddled one here?</i>

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.190
<i>No!</i>

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.440
<i>Being spoiled rotten has 
nothing to do with this...</i>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.190
...and you have even less
to do with this, baseball team!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.360
Hey, Aoyama!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.260
You're gonna start 
taking soccer seriously!

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:59.170
I told you all to <i>get along</i>!

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:00.650
There it is!

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:02.080
Miwa-chan's "ippon seoi nage" throw!

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.170
That's a third dan judo master for you!

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.540
Another clean throw.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:14.180
Why is a judo aficionado even 
coaching the soccer team?

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.520
He jumps out of the way of passes,

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.480
he won't head the ball,

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.670
and any kind of contact play is out.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:29.820
I don't care how talented he is.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.900
I will never accept someone like him!

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.790
Hey, what are you doing?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.640
U-Um, I...

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.710
What was that all about?

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.060
Kaocchi.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.640
Coach?

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:01.100
I really would like you 
to stop calling me that.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.940
What's up?

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.610
I'll take care of locking up
the clubhouse.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:11.230
It's not that. It's about 
Aoyama being a clean freak.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.110
I don't care if
he's a clean freak or whatever.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:18.790
He's either not serious about soccer,
or he just doesn't care.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:19.810
You think so?

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.050
It's obvious!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.500
He'll use wanting to stay clean as an excuse

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.230
to just look on when
the game's hanging in the balance.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:30.440
He won't even touch the ball
without rubber gloves.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.510
You're right about that.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:46.490
After every session, Aoyama cleans 
the balls like that without fail.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.200
Well, sure he does.
He <i>is</i> a clean freak, after all.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.360
But why does he put on 
that ridiculous outfit to do it?

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:57.310
He has to, or else he can't clean the balls.

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:58.820
It's a tremendous handicap.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.870
He can't do what everybody
is able to do naturally.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.950
You sweat and get dirty.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.860
Once the game starts,
you can't avoid contact with others.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.250
It must be rough for a germaphobe.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:17.490
In spite of all that,
he engages in soccer activities every day.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:23.180
Polishing the balls is probably 
like a ritual to him.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:26.140
It's like a "thank you" to the balls.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.500
Aoyama is a true soccer nerd.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.000
<b>Clean Freak! Aoyama-kun</b>

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.990
<b>Hot-Blooded 
Scion! 
Zaizen Kaoru</b>

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.950
<b>Fujimi High School</b>

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.370
So this is Fujimi High School,
 where I'll find Aoyama.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.300
I don't believe this.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.440
Oh, well. It won't matter once I win.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.490
From tomorrow, you'll be part of our team!

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:55.640
That's the famous Oshigami-Minami High.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:00.840
That's Takechi, the guy who was picked 
along with Aoyama for Japan's Under-16s.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.820
He's Tokyo's number one forward.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.550
Thank you.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:07.580
Thank you.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:11.140
I heard they'd only send the reserves...

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:13.230
He's coming this way.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:15.110
Fine by me.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.650
I'll go introduce myself.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.690
Hey! Don't cause any trouble!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:20.850
Hey.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.610
It's been a while, Aoyama!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.080
Takechi-san?

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.180
That over-waxed little gel-head!

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.050
He's actually gelled it really well.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:40.510
Aoyama, why did you reject our invitation?

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.470
This school crashes out
in the district preliminaries every year.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:48.390
You've been given a gift.

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:52.080
So where's the sense in 
letting it go to waste here?

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.850
Hey! What's that supposed to mean?!

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:59.880
I bet you guys can't comprehend
the artistry or true value of Aoyama's game!

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:06.410
I can't allow Aoyama to keep playing
on this team of scrubs.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.160
Just who the hell do you think you are?!

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.390
Don't touch me.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.380
Takechi-san.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:21.580
I came to this school because 
it has something unique about it.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:26.210
Aoyama...

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:31.810
Goal!

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.300
Oshigami-Minami takes the lead!

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.190
Dammit...

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:41.480
What could this team possibly have
that brought you here?

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.070
Will you show me in this match?

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:52.010
Takechi-san, why are you 
showing off your abs?

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:54.260
It's gross. Could you please stop?

00:12:54.820 --> 00:13:01.300
You need a fit, muscular body to get 
you through the rigors of this game!

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:05.260
You want to have a body like mine too, right?

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.190
Aoyama's on the attack!

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:28.910
Close him down!

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.710
R-Right!

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:31.870
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.580
I don't care if you foul him!

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.290
Just stop him in his tracks!

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.070
<i>It's no use. We can't stop him.</i>

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:47.720
<i>I'll just have to...</i>

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:50.520
Huh?

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.670
Keeper!

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.790
<i>He's not shooting?</i>

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.940
<i>You think you can mess around?</i>

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.660
<i>I'll grab it before you get past me!</i>

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:16.750
What?

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.080
Goal!

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.480
Aoyama-kun!

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:30.390
Damn. He made that goal all by himself.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.150
Exquisite.

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:35.960
<i>He didn't let anyone lay a finger on him,</i>

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:38.550
<i>and then he finished it off
with a rabona nutmeg!</i>

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:39.810
<i>That's so like him.</i>

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:43.800
<i>In order to stay out of touching distance
from other players,</i>

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.200
<i>Aoyama's movements are 
frighteningly precise,</i>

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.240
<i>and that's consistently true,
 from start to finish.</i>

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.200
<i>If defenders come near him, 
he dribbles right through them.</i>

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.660
<i>Or he hits a telling one-touch pass.</i>

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:58.250
<i>Fearing this, the defenders 
can't mark him too tightly.</i>

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:01.700
<i>However, if they give him space,</i>

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.170
<i>he has an unrivaled precision shot.</i>

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.900
<i>This is the playing style 
Aoyama arrived at...</i>

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.050
<i>after considering all of 
the things he cannot do.</i>

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:16.040
<i>The germaphobe's absolute domain.</i>

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.920
We took the lead!

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.520
<i>We're a goal up on the 
illustrious Oshigami-Minami.</i>

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.480
Yes, Aoyama! That's goal number two!

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:28.950
<i>I don't want to admit it, 
but he has real skill.</i>

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:31.950
H-He didn't move?

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:38.330
He's really consistent about
not doing anything that'll get him dirty.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.750
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.750
<b>1st     2nd     Total</b>

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.750
<b>Oshigami-
Minami</b>

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:48.680
Takechi-san's on edge because 
we ended the first half 2-1 behind.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:50.400
Tachibana!

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:51.170
Yes!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.720
Did you see Aoyama's almost 
illegally beautiful plays?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.170
He is a veritable<i> treasure</i> 
of Japan's soccer world.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:02.190
Takechi-san, he's still our opponent.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:03.650
I know.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:07.070
We won't let him have his way
in the second half!

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.780
The second half is beginning!

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:18.200
Four defenders marking Aoyama?!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.230
Dammit. There's no way to pass to Aoyama!

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:23.160
Captain!

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:24.620
All right, Tada!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.740
Laughable.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:32.020
As long as Aoyama doesn't get the ball,

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:35.050
Fujimi High has even less bite
than a toothless tiger.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.010
You wish!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.860
Putting four men on Aoyama
gives the rest of us a lot more space!

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:41.330
We'll attack without him!

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.150
There!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.270
Watch this!

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:49.230
Wow, this guy can't use his feet at all.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.470
Ugly. That was too ugly for words.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:55.580
I understand what you're trying to do,

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:58.060
but you know you're not great
with the ball at your feet.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.200
Dammit!

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:08.960
This is bad.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:14.380
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:14.380
<b>1st    2nd      Total</b>

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:14.380
<b>Oshigami-
Minami</b>

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:14.380
Just by shutting down Aoyama, 
the difference is stark.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.500
You get it now, don't you?

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:23.640
This isn't where
you're supposed to be, Aoyama.

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:26.540
It's not too late. Join us.

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.980
Kaocchi! Come here!

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.080
Ten minutes left.

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:35.620
But isn't there something wrong
with Aoyama's movements?

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:37.890
Normally, it doesn't matter how 
many people there are on him.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.410
You're right.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:43.750
It's possible he's injured.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.250
Hey, Aoyama!

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.750
Are you hurt or something?

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:51.450
No.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.560
What gives, then?

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.250
Huh?

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:56.780
Son of a... Look at your feet!

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:01.540
Don't tell me you're just
 avoiding getting dirty!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:05.890
Stop screwing around!

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.440
If you don't want to play, get off the field!

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:18.430
I came to this school because 
it has something unique about it.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:23.120
<i>Why? Why did you come here?!</i>

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.730
<i>In the first half, I actually thought 
you might be serious about soccer.</i>

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.750
<i>But now, you're just...</i>

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:35.670
<i>You disappoint me.</i>

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.590
Last five minutes!

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.340
I got this!

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.930
Oh crap!

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.770
Losers, all of you! This is...

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.400
...the end!

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:00.910
He blocked it with his face?!

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:02.950
Counterattack!

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:07.540
<i>I...</i>

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.970
<i>I don't have the skill or talent Aoyama has.</i>

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.090
<i>But you know what?</i>

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.420
<i>It doesn't matter if the opponent's 
a famous school or not...</i>

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:19.880
<i>I want to win!</i>

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.380
Zaizen!

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:26.680
<i>I'm giving soccer everything I've got here!</i>

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.230
<i>Damn you!</i>

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.220
Goal!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:17.380
I thought you didn't want to get dirty.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:20.990
If it's just the last five minutes,
I can handle it.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.910
I really hate losing.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.820
<i>This guy...</i>

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.660
<i>Aoyama's a clean freak
who has a rod up his ass,</i>

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.510
<i>so to be honest,
I don't like this first-year.</i>

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.380
<b>1st</b>

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.380
<b>2nd</b>

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.380
<b>Total</b>

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.380
<i>But you know what?</i>

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.340
Yippee!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.660
<i>When it comes to the desire to win,
he's just like us.</i>

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:51.720
<i>That makes him a reliable teammate!</i>

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:57.150
Aoyama, you bastard!

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:01.570
Nice header, Zaizen-san.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:09.720
You can have this.

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.450
You're more worthy of the number 10.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:14.910
Zaizen-san...

00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:17.320
I... don't want it.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.270
Put it on!

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:20.910
I'd rather die.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:23.420
Is my shirt that dirty?!

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.960
Aoyama-kun!

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.010
I won't stand for this!

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:31.720
We were supposed to show our superiority
and talk Aoyama into joining us.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.640
But instead, we lost! Unthinkable!

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:37.980
Perhaps I should transfer to Fujimi High.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:39.020
What?

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.900
But I wonder what Aoyama was talking about.

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:45.820
What is so unique about Fujimi High?

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:51.580
I'm glad I came here.

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:56.460
Every toilet needs this feature.

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:32.040
I've decided.

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:35.570
I'm going to support Aoyama-kun
in my own way.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Aoyama-kun, Do You Remember?</b>
